<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariadne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ariadne is a figure of Greek mythology, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minos">King Minos</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, who gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theseus">Theseus</a> the thread that guided him out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labyrinth">Labyrinth</a> after he killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minotaur">Minotaur</a>. Abandoned by Theseus on the island of Naxos, she was found there by the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysus">Dionysus</a>, who made her his wife. She was worshipped as a goddess on Naxos and elsewhere in the Greek world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ariadne.jpg" alt="Ariadne" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dioniso_scopre_arianna,_da_casa_dei_capitelli_colorati_a_pompei,_9278_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
